{
  "_comment": [
    "Gazette S.R.O. 43-Law/2024, 29 February 2024 — the residential tariff immediately before",
    "June 2026, and the proof that the issuing authority changes across the archive: this one is",
    "the Power Division acting under BERC Act s.34ka, the executive route that set tariffs without",
    "a BERC public hearing between January 2023 and August 2024.",
    "",
    "Encoded for BPDB LT-A residential postpaid single-phase only. The gazette fixes one national",
    "LT-A table for all six licensees, but its footnote 3 also carves out BREB's PBSs whose",
    "lifeline rate already exceeds 4.63, and footnote 7 bills PBS consumption at the MT-5 rate.",
    "Encoding the other five utilities without encoding those carve-outs would publish a figure",
    "the gazette does not state, so they are left out.",
    "",
    "Table-2 of this gazette enumerates every permitted miscellaneous fee and every one is a",
    "one-off event charge — no monthly meter rent, no monthly service charge — and its condition",
    "(ka) forbids any charge outside that list. That is why METER_RENT and SERVICE_CHARGE appear",
    "below as NOT applicable rather than as unknowns."
  ],
